    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "You’d like to compare the sprint times between both athletes. The code currently prints the minimum, maximum, and range for each athlete.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n- Compute the mean for Athlete 1 using `statistics.mean`, then print the result.\r\n- Compute the standard deviation for Athlete 1 using `statistics.stdev`, then print the result.\r\n- Compute the mean for Athlete 2 using `statistics.mean`, then print the result.\r\n- Compute the standard deviation for Athlete 2 using `statistics.stdev`, then print the result.\r\n\r\n💻 Coding Tip\r\n\r\nYou can use `round` to round your results to a certain number of decimal points. For example, the following code rounds `value` to two decimal points.\r\n\r\n```\r\nvalue = round(value, 2)\r\n```\r\n",
